# WolkaraForever layer patch 0066 - the unsigned .ipa is a source build, not a reduced one
#
# Why: `package_altstore_ipa.sh` and the release workflow built the published .ipa
# with TOLKARA_SYSTEM_ROOTS=NO, so it carried no macOS system root certificates.
# The Forever client validates Battle.net's certificate against those roots, so
# every login on that artifact was refused with BLZ51900003 - with the
# experimental browser login and without it. The layer now refuses that switch,
# and verify_ipa.sh refuses a package with no root list.
#
# These are the vendored statements that made the reduced build look correct, and
# the Forever instructions that still described the beta (`_classic_beta_`,
# `portal "test"`) after the released client moved to `_forever_` and the launcher
# started writing that config itself. The compatibility table's own rows are left
# as they were measured; the note added above it says which client they describe.
#
# Applies to: AGENTS.md, COMPATIBILITY.md, NOTICE.md, docs/BUILDING.md,
# docs/IPHONE.md, tools/build_emulated_guest.sh, tools/package_ipa.sh,
# .github/workflows/release.yml.
# Upstream: candidate.

