+WoW Forever needs a `portal`, `textLocale` and `audioLocale` in its own
+`_forever_/WTF/Config.wtf`. The launcher writes them when it installs the game
+itself; a copy pushed from a Mac keeps the settings the client saved there.
+Without them the client asks for a region in a window the AppKit adapter cannot
+show, and quits.
 
+It also needs the public system root certificates: the client validates
+Battle.net's certificate against macOS's system roots. A build on your own Mac
+includes them by default (`TOLKARA_SYSTEM_ROOTS=YES`), and the unsigned `.ipa`
+is built with the same inputs, so it carries them too. Login was refused
+(`BLZ51900003`) when either was missing.
+
 ## Input
 
 The [on-screen controls](TOUCH_INPUT.md), a keyboard button and a touch
